:: Bog Cult Intro
You steel yourself and decide to investigate the source of all these strange instances in the bog. Following the beaten wood path, you find that it cuts off abruptly, leaving you with no direction. You cast a glance out into the densely packed trees, attempting to locate a landmark nearby. <<stress 4>><<gstress>>
<br><br>
Suddenly, a <span class="purple">sharp pain resonates within your skull, and your world goes dark.</span>
<br><br>
<<link [[Wake up|Bog Cult Dream]]>><</link>>

:: Bog Cult Dream
<<set $outside to 0>>
You awake bleary-eyed and disoriented, finding yourself in a small wooden room. A flickering florescent light flickers, revealing rotten walls and floorboards. An unknowable black ooze drips from the cracks.
<br><br>
Your furtive look towards the cracks in the wall to find an exit only reveal eyes blinking back at you. You suppress your scream, and scramble away. <<gstress>><<stress 4>>
<br><br>
Tentacles coil around your legs, disrupting your movements and causing you to fall to the floor. <<stress 8>><<ggstress>>
<br><br>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	You struggle for a moment, “P-please, please spare me…” you plead, clasping your hands together.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	You struggle for a moment, “I'm not scared of you!” You kick and squirm around in vain.
<<else>>
	You struggle for a moment, “Let me go!” you shout.
<</if>>
<br><br>
It's only when a voice resonating inside of your head—<span class="purple">No, inside the whole room</span>—whispers to you, your body forcibly going lax, that you finally rest. It speaks in a language you cannot understand but the words alone seem to calm your soul. The tentacles caress your skin, oozing black fluid over your body as the voice slowly fades to silence.
<br><br>
<<if Time.hour lt 22>><<set _passTime to "<<passTimeUntil 22>>">><<set _passTimeDisplay to "0:" + ("0" + ((45 - Time.minute + 60) % 60)).slice(-2)>><</if>>
<<link [[Wake up|Bog Cult Wake]]>>_passTime<</link>>

:: Bog Cult Wake
<<location "bogcult">>
<<set $outside to 0>>
<<npc Salem>><<person1>>
<<if $worn.upper.exposed gte 2 or $worn.lower.exposed gte 2>>
	<<upperwear 79>>
	<<lowerwear 71>>
<</if>>
By the time your eyes open, your surroundings have changed once again. Rotten wood is replaced by cracked stone, and through an unpatched hole in the ceiling you can see the moon hanging high in the sky. The rest of the space doesn't have much to look at, either, the windows covered in bars and a bucket in the corner. It seems to be a cell.
<br><br>
You freeze in place as purple orbs glow in the dark of the room, letting out a shout when they blink. Your attempts to get away are halted by the bindings you've only now realised you were in, keeping you tied down to the bed.<<stress 6>><<gstress>>
<br><br>
A <<personsimple>> scrambles out from the dark, hands waving in front of <<him>> in a flurry of fright, “Wait, wait, wait! I-I can explain, please don't panic!”
<br><br>
<<if $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
    <<link [[Spit at <<him>>|Bog Cult Salem Spit]]>><</link>><<lstress>>
    <br>
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "meek">>
    <<link [[Cower|Bog Cult Salem Cower]]>><</link>><<ltrauma>>
    <br>
<<else>>
    <<link [[Stare|Bog Cult Salem Stare]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Bog Cult Salem Spit
<<He>> jumps back with a small yelp, “I-I'm only trying to help!”
The <<personsimple>> waits stiffly for you to relax, and only moves to help you out of the cuffs when you give <<him>> a curt nod. <<stress -6>>
<br><br>
“I am truly sorry we had to meet like this,” <<He>> frowns, taking a bobby pin from <<his>> hair as <<he>> began to attempt picking at the lock, “M-My name is Salem, I wish we could've talked under… better circumstances.”
<br><br>
You're able to get a better look at Salem now that <<he>>'s closer. <<His>> long black hair blends in with the fabric of <<his>> robes, blanketing you in a sea of darkness, with only <<his>> pale purple eyes standing out against it all, glowing like moonlight. The careful expression you've been watching fades into quiet glee as you both hear a click, the cuffs finally falling free. <<stress -6>><<lstress>>
<br><br>
“I-I did it!” Salem mutters in excitement, moving away from you with haste to get the ones at your feet.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bog Cult Salem After]]>><</link>>

:: Bog Cult Salem Cower
The <<personsimple>> gives you an apologetic look, taking a step back, “S-sorry, May I help you out of those?”
<br><br>
<<He>> awaits your permission, a placating smile on <<his>> face as <<he>> holds <<his>> hands up, showing <<he>> was no threat. At your nod, <<he>> moves to help. <<trauma -6>>
“I am truly sorry we had to meet like this,” <<He>> frowns, taking a bobby pin from <<his>> hair as <<he>> began to attempt picking at the lock, “M-My name is Salem, I wish we could've talked under… better circumstances.”
<br><br>
You're able to get a better look at Salem now that <<he>>'s closer. <<His>> long black hair blends in with the fabric of <<his>> robes, blanketing you in a sea of darkness, with only <<his>> pale purple eyes standing out against it all, glowing like moonlight. The careful expression you've been watching fades into quiet glee as you both hear a click, the cuffs finally falling free. <<stress -6>><<lstress>>
<br><br>
“I-I did it!” Salem mutters in excitement, moving away from you with haste to get the ones at your feet.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bog Cult Salem After]]>><</link>>

:: Bog Cult Salem Stare
<<He>> quietly approaches, caution in <<his>> steps as <<he>> leans over you.
“I am truly sorry we had to meet like this,” <<He>> frowns, taking a bobby pin from <<his>> hair as <<he>> began to attempt picking at the lock, “M-My name is Salem, I wish we could've talked under… better circumstances.”
<br><br>
You're able to get a better look at Salem now that <<he>>'s closer. <<His>> long black hair blends in with the fabric of <<his>> robes, blanketing you in a sea of darkness, with only <<his>> pale purple eyes standing out against it all, glowing like moonlight. The careful expression you've been watching fades into quiet glee as you both hear a click, the cuffs finally falling free. <<stress -6>><<lstress>>
<br><br>
“I-I did it!” Salem mutters in excitement, moving away from you with haste to get the ones at your feet.
