:: Bog Cult Salem After
Salem gingerly helps you sit up, concern written on <<his>> face, “I promise we're not bad people, T-The Fellowship is just heavily guarded. The elders sensed your presence encroaching onto temple territory, so they, um.”
<br><br>
Salem bites <<his>> lip, wringing <<his>> hands together to try and exorcise <<his>> nerves.
<br><br>
“T-The Fellowship is the true religion of the town, that other group currently taking residence in our old temple are heretic defectors! …As the elders have told me,” <<he>> continued, <<his>> voice growing steadier as <<he>> spoke, his belief clearly unwavering, “Our ancestors were banished from town without a rhyme or reason. Our ceremonies may look dangerous, but we wouldn't hurt a soul!”
<br><br>
<<He>> gets up abruptly, <<his>> composure faltering as <<he>> stands face to face with you.
<br><br>
“A-anyway, If you would please follow me,” Salem straightens <<his>> shoulders with feigned confidence, “There is something I'd like to show you.”
<br><br>
<<link [[Next (0:10)|Bog Cult Salem Intro]]>><<pass 10>><</link>>

:: Bog Cult Salem Intro
Salem peeks out of the cell entryway, motioning for you to follow along as soon as the coast is clear.
<br><br>
<<His>> footsteps are hurried, you struggle to follow <<him>> through the winding temple halls. Salem occasionally looks behind <<himself>> to make sure <<he>> hasn't lost you.
<br><br>
“Don't worry, it seems like a lot at first, b-but I'm sure you'll get used to it soon,” <<he>> assures, breaking the silence. <<He>> turns away quickly as you shoot <<him>> a confused look.
<br><br>
Soon, the maze of halls gives way to a large, dimly lit room. Flickering candle light illuminates the altar beyond the rows of pews.
<br><br>
“This is our temple's chapel. We, um, pray and hold mass here every Sunday.” <<He>> gestures around awkwardly, standing back with <<his>> hands clasped in front of <<himself>>. <<He>> looks like <<he>> has something to say.
<br><br>
<<if $speech_attitude is "meek">>
	“Are you alright? You look nervous,” you say, trying to coax <<him>> out of <<his>> shell.
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
	“Well? Out with it.” you snap, causing <<him>> to startle.
<<else>>
	You raise a brow at <<him>>, waiting for <<him>> to continue.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<He>> lets out a deep sigh, looking at the ground, “Can we speak, Privately? I have an idea to… um.” Salem leans in close, putting <<his>> hand up to your ear, “I want to help you get out of here.”
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bog Cult Salem Next]]>><</link>>

:: Bog Cult Salem Next
<<He>> leads you down another hall, this one covered with doors as far as you can see. <<He>> only halts when you both reach the end of it in front of a decrepit door, much like any other in here.
<br><br>
“This is it…” <<he>> heaves out a breath, slowly turning the doorknob. The area you see looks similar to the cell you were in.
<br><br>
It's only set apart by the various vines growing out of the cracks, with flowers blooming in a myriad of shades. There are two beds in there, one with merely a sheet and pillow, and the other an eclectic assembly of torn sheets and blankets. There's potted plants littered around the corners of the room, and you notice a well used bookshelf between the two beds.
<br><br>
“This is my room,” <<he>> explains, scratching the back of <<his>> neck as <<he>> shifts on <<his>> feet. Soon, Salem opens the door further, making space for you, “W-Would you like to come in?”
<br><br>
<<link [[Enter|Bog Cult Salem Next Again]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<if $promiscuity gte 15>>
    <<link [[Flirt|Bog Cult Salem Flirt Intro]]>><</link>>
<</if>>

:: Bog Cult Salem Flirt Intro
<<if $speech_attitude is "bratty">>
    “You're skipping a few steps…” you goad, “Most people beg to see me in their room first.” You walk past <<him>>, squeezing <<his>> thin bicep. <<He>> gapes at you in shock.<<stress -6>><<lstress>>
<<elseif $speech_attitude is "meek">>
    “I didn't take you for that kind of person, Salem,” you mumble coyly, “I guess looks can be deceiving?” You brush past <<him,>> your hand gently skimming <<his>> shoulder. <<He>> takes pause, looking at <<his>> shoulder, then back at you. <<stress -6>><<lstress>>
<<else>> 
    “Oh wow, you're forward, aren't you?” you tease, squeezing <<his>> shoulder as you pass. <<He>> takes pause, fixing you with a confused stare until the realisation sets in.<<stress -6>><<lstress>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
“T-That is most certainly not w-what I invited you here for!” <<he>> retorts, <<his>> voice dry and dying out by the end. It's clear you caught <<him>> off guard. <<He>> covers <<his>> flushed face and retreats to <<his>> side of the room. <<lust 3>>
<br><br>
Salem sits on <<his>> bed, posture stiff as <<he>> pulls <<his>> knees to <<his>> chest, “T-This is so awkward, I've never let anyone in here before,” <<he>> whispers, embarrassed as <<his>> hands dig into the skirt of <<his>> robe, “B-But it's really important, because I have a plan. The elders won't let us leave if you know about our existence, but becoming an initiate should fix that! Then you'll be able to come and go as you like!”
<br><br>
You notice <<his>> anxieties take a backseat when <<he>>'s got a set goal in mind, <<his>> words far more confident as <<he>> explains, “The ceremony is actually pretty simple. Just an altar and some… um… Wax? I don't remember my own, but I remember it not hurting that much, so you should be fine!”
<br><br>
You don't really share the same confidence <<he>> does.
<br><br>
“Just… let me know when you're ready to go,” <<he>> smiles sheepishly, turning away from you as <<he>> begins to meditate.
<br><br>
<<salemroomicon>><<link [[Next|Bog Cult Salem Room]]>><</link>>

