:: Bog Cult Salem Plant
The plants seem to be of all types. You can spot Asters and Vervain among other more dangerous species like Nightshade. You probably shouldn't touch them.
<br><br>
<<salemroomicon>><<link [[Back|Bog Cult Salem Room]]>><</link>>

:: Bog Cult Salem Read
You skim the bookshelf for anything interesting, landing on a book named "Magnus Liber Ultra". The pages are pristine and sharp, standing out against the old run down temple building, it piques your curiosity.
<br><br>
Opening it up, it seems to be an old diary of sorts. It documents the daily life of an unnamed author searching for the truth of the universe. By the end of the book, the author writes of their untimely demise and their prayers to preserve the knowledge they held inside their diary. You note that a few pages are torn out.
<br><br>
You assume misfortune must've fallen on the original sector that would become 'The Fellowship'.
<br><br>
<<salemroomicon>><<link [[Back|Bog Cult Salem Room]]>><</link>>

:: Bog Cult Salem Initiation
<<npc Salem>><<person1>>
“Are you ready to begin?” <<He>> asks, surprisingly stoic despite his past behaviour. It seems like his meditation gave <<him>> time to prepare <<himself>>, “Please, follow after me.”
<br><br>
<<link [[Back|Bog Cult Salem Beg]]>><</link>>

:: Bog Cult Salem Beg
Salem leads you back down the same corridor, not looking back to check on you this time. Luckily, you manage to keep pace. <<He>> leads you back into the main hall, hands behind his back as <<he>> bows before the elders.
<br><br>
“Honorable elders,” <<He>> greets, lowering to <<his>> knees and prostrating <<himself>> before them, “Forgive me for my insolence, for I have taken it upon myself to speak with the interloper and have reached my own conclusion of <<pher>> fate. It is with great humility that I request we take <<phim>> in as one of our own rather than risk any alternative.”
<br><br>
<<if $churchsalemtold>>
“N-Not to mention, <<pshe>>… is one of <i>theirs</i>… Should <<pshe>> be missing for too long, I-I fear they may come searching.”
<br><br>
The elders stare down at Salem, mumbling amongst themselves.
<br><br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Next|Bog Cult Salem Ritual Intro]]>><</link>>

:: Bog Cult Salem Ritual Intro
“Salem.” The voice that speaks up is raspy, coming from one of the elders, “You are correct, your insolence bodes consequence, but we do find merit in what you speak of.”
<br><br>
Another elder raises their hand, stepping forward, “<<pShe>> shall undergo the initiation ritual as suggested.. However, your punishment for going behind your elder’s back shall be carried out swiftly.”
<br><br>
Salem’s forehead pressed deep into the stone, “T-Thank you, Honorable elders. I will not forget your mercy.”
<br><br>
<<He>> is soon ushered away by two nuns. <<He>> looks back at you, a small smile on his face as he nods at you.
<br><br>
You turn your attention to the elders, all of whom have set their sights directly on you.<<stress 4>><<gstress>>
<br><br>
"You, child.” One of them points a bony finger at you, the rest splitting away from the altar to make space, “Lie herein, upon our altar, and you shall be reborn through our God.”
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bog Cult Salem Ritual Start]]>><</link>>

:: Bog Cult Salem Ritual Start
The elders crowd around you, placing cloth over your head and obscuring your vision.
<br><br>
An ice cold fear seizes you as they begin to displace your clothes, your limbs being forcibly held down as your skin is exposed to the chilly air of the temple. <<stress 4>><<gstress>>
<br><br>
You jolt with alarm as something drips onto your skin, searing hot at first, and then quickly cooling against you. This must be the wax Salem had mentioned beforehand. <<pain 4>><<gpain>>
<br><br>
You grit your teeth, fighting back against the tears welling in your eyes as your hands clench into fists. This lasts several minutes before you feel the hands on you retreat and the cloth is pulled off your face.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bog Cult Salem Ritual End]]>><</link>>

:: Bog Cult Salem Ritual End
The elders are seemingly done with you, going about their regular duties aside from a single one who waited for you. You hastily fix your clothes, prying off bits of wax as you go.
<br><br>
“You shall be rooming with Salem,” The elder informs you, “<<He>> must take responsibility for your tutelage as part of his own consequences. Behave, and you shall not face any troubles here.”
<br><br>
With that, they leave you alone for the time being. You can explore the temple if you wish.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Bog Cult]]>><<set $cultjoined to 1>><<set $salempunishment to 1>><<set $salemgone to 1>><<endevent>><</link>>

