:: Salem Arcade
    <<npc Salem>><<person1>>
    As you and Salem make your way into town, <<he>> begins to slightly hide behind you. You let <<him>> trail slightly as you pass the hospital. <<He>> peers at the injured people with interest as you continue down Oxford and finally arrive on Starfish Street. You open the arcade door, are hit with cool air conditioning, and walk in with Salem right behind.
    <br><br>
    <<if $salemarcade is 1>>
        As you enter, Salem has already began to relax, away from prying eyes. <<He>> slowly lets go of your arm and looks at the arcade cabinets. Without waiting for your input, <<he>> pulls you toward a newer one. "Hey look at this one." <<He>> smiles warmly at you. "Do you want to try playing with me? I have been practicing in my head for this moment."
        <br><br>
        You and Salem spend some time playing games together. <<He>> is still pretty bad at games but you are surprised to see <<him>> manage to take a game off you. As <<he>> catches sight of the clock, <<his>> face sinks a little. "I-is it already that time?" <<He>> looks worried. "S-sorry I have to get back to the Fellowship before my duties."
        <br><br>
        Salem reaches out <<his>> hand to take yours as the two of you return down the path back to the Fellowship, sneaking Salem back to <<his>> room and closing the door gently.
        <br><br>
        <<salemroomicon>><<link [[Next|Bog Cult Salem Room]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
    <<else>>
        The arcade is mostly empty which causes Salem to relax. <<He>> slowly lets go of your arm and looks at the arcade cabinets. Curiously Salem touches one and tilts <<his>> head. "What are these things? Are they kind of like a television?" You take a moment to explain what an arcade is and Salem looks dumbfounded. "W-wait so it's like a television that you control what happens on the glass? That's so cool!"
        <br><br>
        You and Salem spend some time playing games together after you teach <<him>> the controls. <<He>> pretty quickly learns but not enough to actually win anything. Despite this, <<he>> seems to be having fun. "I-is it already that time?" <<He>> looks worried. "S-sorry I have to get back to the Fellowship before my duties."
        <br><br>
        Salem reaches out <<his>> hand to take yours as the two of you return down the path back to the Fellowship, sneaking Salem back to <<his>> room and closing the door gently.
